{"availability":"available","full":"wasi-master/wmkeyboard","name":"wmkeyboard","description":"A modern, privacy-first Android keyboard: offline intelligence, 600+ languages, themes, tools and an addon ecosystem.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Kotlin","stars":552,"forks":27,"created":"2026-08-10T12:14:22Z","updated":"2026-10-14T18:04:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wmkeyboard.pages.dev","topics":["android","bengali","ime","input-method","jetpack-compose","keyboard","kotlin","material-you","privacy"],"demo":"https://wmkeyboard.pages.dev/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.652Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.652Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.652Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T01:10:19.562Z","stars":503,"forks":22},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:16:21.109Z","stars":531,"forks":26},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.652Z","stars":552,"forks":27}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An open source multilingual Android keyboard with prediction, glide typing, transliteration, emoji search and a 75+ tool toolbox that all run on the phone and never phone home.","A keyboard is the one app that sees everything you write. Your messages, your passwords, your half-typed thoughts you deleted before sending. Somewhere along the way the popular keyboards decided that was a business model. The prediction got better, and the price for that was a copy of your keystrokes getting sent to somebody else's server.","The keyboards that refused that deal were mostly forks of the same decade-old Android code. Good bones, honest intentions, but no glide typing without a proprietary blob, no real toolbox, and nothing for the language I actually type in. Bangla was an afterthought everywhere: either a phonetic engine bolted on with no prediction, or a layout with no smart features behind it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wasi-master/wmkeyboard/blob/main/README.md","finge